======================================================================
 XBat CLI v1.1.0.0 - Batch Script to Executable Compiler
======================================================================

Usage:
  XBatC.exe /bat <BatScriptPath> [options...]

Required Arguments:
  /bat <path>        Path to the source batch file (.bat / .cmd) to compile.

Optional Output Settings:
  /exe <path>        Path to the target output executable (.exe).
                     (Default: generated in the same dir with the same name as source batch)
  /x64               Build a native 64-bit executable.
                     (Default: build 32-bit x86 executable)
  /upx               Compress the final executable using UPX.
                     (WARNING: UPX may cause problems, including resource fails. Be careful to use it.)

Execution Modes:
  /mode <type>       Set payload execution backend environment. Supported modes:
                       standard : Extracts assets to dropdir and runs securely. (Default)
                       memory   : Pure in-memory streaming execution via pipes.
                       (WARNING: memory mode is experimental and does NOT support
                       interactive commands, e.g. pause or set /p.)
                       lite     : Simple script execution without creating a pipe.
  /invisible         Hide the application console window on payload startup.
                     (Default: console window is visible)

Resource & Cleanup Options:
  /include <path>    Include external user resource files or directories.
                     (Can be specified multiple times to package multiple folders)
  /icon <path>       Inject custom .ico application icon into the target EXE.
  /ver <path>        Inject custom PE version information via an .ini file template.
  /dropdir <int>     Set the drop extraction target location for standard mode:
                       0 : User's local %TEMP% directory. (Default)
                       1 : Current execution directory.
  /noclean           Disable post-execution asset cleanup.
                     (Default: completely purges session data on exit)

======================================================================
 IMPORTANT: SCRIPT DEVELOPMENT ENVIRONMENT GUIDE
======================================================================
  1. SCRIPT ENCODING WARNING (CRITICAL):
     The source batch file MUST be saved in native ANSI encoding (e.g., GBK for
     Chinese Windows, Code Page 936). Do NOT use UTF-8! UTF-8 scripts containing
     non-ASCII characters will cause messy code and runtime failures.

  2. WORKPATH & PATH LOCATOR:
     DO NOT use '%~dp0' in your batch script to locate files! Due to the isolated
     and in-memory extraction backend, '%~dp0' will point to incorrect temp dirs.

     Use these pre-injected XBat Environment Variables instead:
       %EXEDIR%    Points to the TRUE physical directory where the compiled EXE resides.
       %RESDIR%    Points to the directory containing all your /include assets.

     Example inside script:
       copy "%RESDIR%\config.dat" "%APPDATA%\"
       echo Current Wrapper EXE location is: %EXEDIR%

Examples:
  1. Standard Mode compilation with hidden window:
     XBatC.exe /bat run.bat /exe output.exe /invisible

  2. Heavy packing with assets, custom icon, metadata injection and x64 payload:
     XBatC.exe /bat build.bat /exe final.exe /mode standard /x64
                   /include .\my_assets /icon app.ico /ver version.ini

  3. Pure in-memory high-protection pipe execution:
     XBatC.exe /bat core_logic.bat /exe secured.exe /mode memory

======================================================================